{"severity":"error","file":"errors/linear_generic_param_8.march","start_line":12,"start_col":4,"end_line":12,"end_col":13,"message":"`RingBuf(a)` is linear, but `Vault.set` is generic in a parameter of that type, so it may drop or duplicate the value.\nConsume the value here instead, or, if `Vault.set` uses that parameter exactly once, mark it `linear` where `Vault.set` is defined (`linear x : a`).","code":"linear_generic_param","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[]}
